# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Added after the SALP -> SLAP rename: copying the working tree flipped
# every tracked file to CRLF, and `git status` reported all 62 of them as
# modified with 30,513 insertions and 30,513 deletions. A real one-line
# change would have been invisible in that. `text=auto` stores LF in the
# object database regardless of what the working tree does, so the same
# accident cannot produce a phantom diff again.
#
# Working trees are left alone (no `eol=` here), so Windows checkouts keep
# whatever core.autocrlf says locally.
* text=auto

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.gz     binary
*.zip    binary
*.sqlite3 binary

# Shell scripts and anything a Linux runner executes must be LF even if
# checked out on Windows, or the shebang line carries a CR and the kernel
# reports "bad interpreter".
*.sh     text eol=lf

# Batch files are the mirror image: CRLF or cmd.exe can misparse them.
*.bat    text eol=crlf
*.cmd    text eol=crlf
